From 97c7bd469dfb57f74cfc54fff1800ff1654f06ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:27:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gresolv: Return 0 when g_resolv_lookup_hostname()
 cannot send a query

g_resolv_lookup_hostname() returns a guint lookup id, and 0 means no
lookup was started; the early returns for a failed allocation already
use it. When the A or AAAA query could not be sent (no nameserver could
be reached, or out of memory) it returned -EIO instead, which reaches
the caller as 4294967291. gweb's do_request() took that for a running
lookup, queued the session and returned a request id, but no result
callback would ever come for it: the MMS transfer neither completed nor
failed. Return 0 so that the caller sees the failure.

ConnMan's gresolv still returns -EIO here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 gweb/gresolv.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gweb/gresolv.c b/gweb/gresolv.c
index f32106d..5b19220 100644
--- a/gweb/gresolv.c
+++ b/gweb/gresolv.c
@@ -1036,7 +1036,7 @@ guint g_resolv_lookup_hostname(GResolv *resolv, const char *hostname,
 	if (resolv->result_family != AF_INET6) {
 		if (add_query(lookup, hostname, ns_t_a)) {
 			g_free(lookup);
-			return -EIO;
+			return 0;
 		}
 	}
 
@@ -1049,7 +1049,7 @@ guint g_resolv_lookup_hostname(GResolv *resolv, const char *hostname,
 			}
 
 			g_free(lookup);
-			return -EIO;
+			return 0;
 		}
 	}
 
